From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:06:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Wake an idle dedicated worker when it is terminated

`Worker::terminate` sets the worker's closing flag and requests an interrupt,
but the interrupt only stops running script. A worker that is waiting for its
next message stays blocked in its event loop and only checks the closing flag
after it receives something, so its thread, runtime and global stayed alive,
together with its nested workers.

Send the `WakeUp` message that the worker event loop already handles.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit f2e87c24b04150eb5ee3aab7cfef1dab81a25405)

----

Fork note: the owner's commit from the branch servo-leaks-worker-terminate, not
upstream yet, cherry-picked without conflicts for the IndexedDB redesign. Since
"script: Close a worker's IndexedDB connections when its event loop ends", the
end of a worker's event loop also runs its IndexedDB teardown, so a terminated
idle worker now aborts its transactions and closes its connections at once
instead of when its next message arrives, and its writer no longer holds back
the database. The fork part removes the FAIL expectation of
IndexedDB/transaction-inflight-worker-terminate.window.js. Drop this patch once
the commit lands upstream; keep the expectation change.

Validation: build host release with SpiderMonkey and with QuickJS, then run IndexedDB/transaction-inflight-worker-terminate.window.html, IndexedDB/worker-termination-aborts-upgrade.window.html and /_mozilla/mozilla/worker-terminate-idle.html with --repeat 3: all pass 3 of 3 on both engines, while the 92b5f086e08 binary (SM) fails the first and the third 3 of 3 ("transaction never settled", "the nested worker stopped"); host SM IndexedDB/ 4,483 of 4,511 with the new pass as the only unexpected result (92b5f086e08: 4,482), /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ 306 of 306
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent cherry-picked commit f2e87c24b04 onto the IndexedDB redesign branch, removed the fixed test's expectation and measured the effect on both engines)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
